/*  Types a module carries — `ModuleTypeLifting` in `src/Interpreter/ModuleTypeLifting.cs`.

    ★ A front-end pass, run before anything else is checked. Each type a module carries is moved
    out to the top level under a name nobody can write — `span in spans`, unwritable for its space
    — and every reference to the short name inside the module and its carried types is rewritten
    to match. So the hoist meets an ordinary top-level object, and only a `Pull` of the module puts
    the short name back in scope, as a scoped type, for the length of its block.

    ★ Inside a `Pull` of such a module the short name is rewritten too, so a DECLARATION in the
    block can name the type in its signature — unless the block declares a type of that name
    itself, which then wins.

    ⚠ Only the program's top-level statements are lifted, and only top-level pulls (and the pulls
    inside them) are rewritten, as C# does.
*/

Pull a book on collections.
    /// The name to SHOW for a type: the one its author wrote, any owner appended taken back off —
    /// trimmed at the LAST ` in `, so a carried generic keeps the part that is really its name.
    Bind text to display-name, given (the text name):
        Define letters as a chase.
        Insert name into letters.
        Define at as 0.
        Define place as 1.
        While place + 3 is not greater than the number of letters, repeat:
            If item place of letters is " " and item (place + 1) of letters is "i" and item (place + 2) of letters is "n"
                    and item (place + 3) of letters is " ":
                The at becomes place.
            Done.
            Increment place by 1.
        Done.
        If at is not greater than 1, return name.
        Define kept as a chase.
        Define index as 1.
        While index is less than at, repeat:
            Insert item index of letters into kept.
            Increment index by 1.
        Done.
        Return kept converted to text.
    Done.

    /// A copy of `whole` with its `place`th field replaced.
    Bind node to with-field, given (the node whole, the number place, the node value):
        Define copy as a new node { the kind whole's kind, the word whole's word, the children a series of node }.
        Define index as 0.
        For each child in whole's children, repeat:
            Increment index by 1.
            If index is place, cast copy's add on (value).
            Otherwise, cast copy's add on (child).
        Done.
        Return copy.
    Done.

    /// A copy of `shape` with every object type and object literal named in `names` renamed.
    Bind node to renamed-deep, given (the node shape, the map from text to text names):
        If shape's kind is "atom", return shape.
        Define copy as a new node { the kind shape's kind, the word shape's word, the children a series of node }.
        Define index as 0.
        Define renames as shape's kind is "ObjectType" or shape's kind is "ObjectLiteral".
        For each child in shape's children, repeat:
            Increment index by 1.
            Define replaced as false.
            If renames and index is 1:
                Define lifted as the entry for (cast unquoted on (child) in lowercase) in names.
                If lifted is not void:
                    Cast copy's add on (cast quoted on (lifted)).
                    The replaced becomes true.
                Done.
            Done.
            If replaced is false, cast copy's add on (cast renamed-deep on (child, names)).
        Done.
        Return copy.
    Done.

    /// `ModuleTypeLifting.Expand`: the program with every carried type lifted to the top level.
    Bind node to lift-carried-types unto checker, given (the node program):
        Define rewritten as cast listed.
        Define any as false.
        For each statement in program's children, repeat:
            Define held as cast listed.
            If statement's kind is "ObjectDefinition", the held becomes cast field-of on (statement, 13).
            If held's kind is "list" and the number of held's children is greater than 0:
                The any becomes true.
                Define module-name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)).
                Define names as a map from text to text.
                For each type in held's children, repeat:
                    Define short as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (type, 1)).
                    In names, the entry for (short in lowercase) becomes "{short} in {module-name}".
                Done.
                For each type in held's children, repeat:
                    Define renamed as cast renamed-deep on (cast with-field on (type, 13, cast listed), names).
                    Define short as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (type, 1)).
                    Cast rewritten's add on (cast with-field on (renamed, 1, cast quoted on ("{short} in {module-name}"))).
                Done.
                Cast rewritten's add on (cast renamed-deep on (cast with-field on (statement, 13, cast listed), names)).
                In one's carried-types, the entry for (module-name in lowercase) becomes names.
            Done.
            Otherwise:
                Cast rewritten's add on (statement).
            Done.
        Done.
        If any is false, return program.
        Return cast one's rewrite-inside-pulls on (rewritten).
    Done.

    /// Inside `Pull <module>. … Done.`, the module's carried short names are rewritten to their
    /// lifted ones — except a name the block declares a type of itself.
    Bind node to rewrite-inside-pulls unto checker, given (the node statements):
        Define result as cast listed.
        For each statement in statements's children, repeat:
            If statement's kind is not "PullStatement":
                Cast result's add on (statement).
            Done.
            Otherwise:
                Define own as a series of node.
                Cast gather-kind on (cast field-of on (statement, 2), "ObjectDefinition", own).
                Define declared as a map from text to fact.
                For each definition in own, repeat:
                    In declared, the entry for (cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (definition, 1)) in lowercase) becomes true.
                Done.
                Define names as a map from text to text.
                Define count as 0.
                For each pair in (cast field-of on (statement, 1))'s children, repeat:
                    Define book as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (pair, 1)).
                    Define mine as the entry for (book in lowercase) in one's carried-types.
                    If mine is not void:
                        For each entry in mine, repeat:
                            If (the entry for (the key of entry) in declared) is void:
                                In names, the entry for (the key of entry) becomes the value of entry.
                                Increment count by 1.
                            Done.
                        Done.
                    Done.
                Done.
                Define body as cast field-of on (statement, 2).
                If count is greater than 0, the body becomes cast renamed-deep on (body, names).
                The body becomes cast one's rewrite-inside-pulls on (body).
                Cast result's add on (cast with-field on (statement, 2, body)).
            Done.
        Done.
        Return result.
    Done.

    /// "", or why this pull is beyond reach: C# also puts a carried type's short name in SCOPE for
    /// the block, which reaches a pull the rewrite above did not — one inside an `If`, say. This
    /// checker resolves only the rewritten names, so a short name still standing is not judged.
    Bind text to carried-beyond-reach unto checker, given (the node statement):
        Define names as a map from text to fact.
        For each pair in (cast field-of on (statement, 1))'s children, repeat:
            Define mine as the entry for (cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (pair, 1)) in lowercase) in one's carried-types.
            If mine is not void:
                For each entry in mine, repeat:
                    In names, the entry for (the key of entry) becomes true.
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
        If the size of names is 0, return "".
        Define own as a series of node.
        Cast gather-kind on (cast field-of on (statement, 2), "ObjectDefinition", own).
        For each definition in own, repeat:
            If (the entry for (cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (definition, 1)) in lowercase) in names) is not void:
                Return "a block declaring a type its pull carries".
            Done.
        Done.
        For each wanted in a series with ("ObjectType", "ObjectLiteral"), repeat:
            Define found as a series of node.
            Cast gather-kind on (cast field-of on (statement, 2), wanted, found).
            For each reference in found, repeat:
                If (the entry for (cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (reference, 1)) in lowercase) in names) is not void:
                    Return "a carried type named inside a pull that is not at the top level".
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
        Return "".
    Done.
Done.
